Copyright (c) 2026 Aloha Pixel. All rights reserved.

This agreement is between Aloha Pixel ("we", "us") and you, the person or
company that purchased a license for the Reef theme (the "Theme"). By
downloading, installing or using the Theme you accept these terms. If you do
not accept them, do not use the Theme.

1. WHAT THE THEME IS

The Theme is the source code, styles, components, scripts, documentation and
demo content distributed under the name "Reef". Fonts and other third-party
components bundled with the Theme are listed in THIRD-PARTY.md and remain
governed by their own licenses; this agreement covers everything else.

2. WHAT YOU MAY DO

Subject to this agreement, we grant you a non-exclusive, non-transferable,
worldwide, perpetual license to:

a. Use the Theme to build an unlimited number of end products, for yourself,
   your company or your clients. An "end product" is a website or web
   application whose purpose is its own content or service, not the Theme
   itself: a SaaS marketing site, a product site, a company site, a client
   project.
b. Modify the Theme without limit: rebrand it, restructure it, delete from it,
   extend it. Modified code stays subject to this agreement.
c. Deploy end products commercially or non-commercially, on any number of
   domains, with no attribution required.
d. Keep the Theme source in the private repositories of the end products that
   use it, accessible to the people working on those products.

3. ONE LICENSE PER DEVELOPER

Each license covers one developer: one person who edits the Theme source.
A team of three people editing the source needs three licenses. People who
only view the deployed end product, write content in it, or review work
without editing the Theme source do not need a license. A license is tied to
a person, not a machine: your licensed developer may work on any number of
computers.

4. WHAT YOU MAY NOT DO

a. Redistribute the Theme as a theme. You may not resell, sublicense, share,
   publish or give away the Theme, in whole or in substantial part, as a
   theme, template, starter, boilerplate, UI kit, component library or
   similar developer-facing product, whether free or paid, modified or not.
   This is the one thing this license protects.
b. Publish the Theme source in a public repository or any location where
   people without a license can obtain it. Open sourcing an end product that
   embeds the Theme requires removing the Theme or contacting us for a
   written exception.
c. Extract components, styles or documentation from the Theme to build a
   competing developer-facing product.
d. Transfer or resell your license, except that a company may reassign a
   seat from a developer who leaves to the developer who replaces them.
e. Use the Theme in an end product whose primary value is the Theme itself,
   such as a site generator that outputs Reef-based sites for third parties
   without each recipient holding a license.

5. DEMO CONTENT

The demo copy, the fictional publication "Reef Notes", its fictional authors
and articles are part of the Theme and are provided for
demonstration. Replace them in production; do not present fictional
testimonials or ratings as real.

6. UPDATES AND SUPPORT

Your purchase includes access to updates of the major version you bought.
Support, when offered, is provided on a reasonable-effort basis and is not a
guaranteed service level. We may release new major versions under separate
terms.

